@node Table readers
@section Table readers

The table readers are generated from s-expression schemas in
@file{otf/schemas/}, derived from the Fontations table definitions, by
the code generator in @file{otf/codegen/}; the generated code is in
@file{otf/src/tables/}.  To change a reader, change its schema or the
generator and run @command{make codegen}.  Every table follows the same
naming:

@table @code
@item (read-@var{table} @var{font-data} @var{offset} &optional @var{length})
Check the table's fixed part and return a view of it, a structure named
@var{table}.  For example @code{read-head}, @code{read-hhea},
@code{read-cmap}.
@item (@var{table}-@var{field} @var{view})
A field, decoded.  @code{(head-units-per-em head)}.
@item (@var{table}-@var{field}-raw @var{font-data} @var{offset})
The same field read straight from the bytes, without a view.
@item (@var{table}-@var{array}-count @var{view})
@itemx (@var{table}-@var{array}-ref @var{view} @var{index})
The length and the elements of an array field.
@item (@var{flags}-@var{flag}-p @var{flags})
A bit of a flags field.
@item +@var{table}-tag+
@itemx +@var{record}-size+
The table's tag and the size of a fixed record, as constants.
@end table

Every view includes @code{table-ref} (with @code{table-ref-font-data},
@code{table-ref-offset}, @code{table-ref-length}), and every record
@code{record-ref}.  Offsets inside a table are followed with
@code{resolve-offset16}, @code{resolve-offset32} and their
@code{nullable} versions.

The tables of a font are found through its table directory:

@lisp
(let* ((fd (otf:ensure-font-data #p"DejaVuSans.ttf"))
       (td (otf:read-table-directory fd 0)))
  (dotimes (i (otf:table-directory-table-records-count td))
    (let ((rec (otf:table-directory-table-records-ref td i)))
      (when (string= (otf:table-record-tag rec) "head")
        (return (otf:head-units-per-em
                 (otf:read-head fd (otf:table-record-offset rec)
                                (otf:table-record-length rec))))))))
@end lisp

A collection starts with a @code{ttc-header} instead
(@code{read-ttc-header}), whose
@code{ttc-header-table-directory-offsets-ref} gives each font's table
directory.

Tables with readers include the core TrueType tables (@samp{head},
@samp{hhea}, @samp{hmtx}, @samp{maxp}, @samp{name}, @samp{OS/2},
@samp{post}, @samp{cmap}, @samp{glyf}, @samp{kern}), the layout tables
(@samp{GDEF}, @samp{GSUB}, @samp{GPOS}, @samp{BASE}, @samp{MATH}), the
variation tables (@samp{fvar}, @samp{avar}, @samp{gvar}, @samp{cvar},
@samp{HVAR}, @samp{VVAR}, @samp{MVAR}, @samp{STAT}), colour and bitmap
tables (@samp{COLR}, @samp{CPAL}, @samp{CBDT}, @samp{CBLC}, @samp{EBDT},
@samp{EBLC}, @samp{sbix}, @samp{SVG }) and the Apple tables
(@samp{morx}, @samp{kerx}, @samp{feat}, @samp{trak}, @samp{ankr} and
others).  @file{otf/doc/font-loader-details.md} lists them and the
tables left out.

A few layouts whose shape depends on the data itself are decoded by
hand in @file{otf/src/extensions.lisp}, for example
@code{fvar-axis-ref}, @code{fvar-instance-ref},
@code{gvar-glyph-variation-data-header}, @code{read-gpos-value-record},
@code{pair-set-pair-value-record-ref}, @code{mvar-value-record-ref} and
@code{strike-glyph-data}.  Their docstrings describe them.

@node Web fonts
@section Web fonts

WOFF compresses each table with zlib; WOFF2 compresses all of them with
Brotli and transforms @samp{glyf}, @samp{loca} and @samp{hmtx}.  Both are
decoded with the @code{decompress} system.  @code{open-font-loader}
recognises them by itself; these functions decode them explicitly.

@defun decode-woff1 source &key verify-checksums
